# Transcript translation (D3)

When editing files matched by this rule:

1. **Read first:** `skills/transcript-translation/SKILL.md` and `docs/d3-transcript-translation-roadmap.md`.
2. **Canonical language:** Persist transcripts and APX-03 output in English. Translations are derived artifacts keyed by `target_locale`.
3. **Token budget:** Use `src/lib/transcript-translation/token-budget.ts` before sending transcript text to any LLM. Never pass an unbounded transcript to `SessionAgent` or a translation call.
4. **LLM stack:** Extend `src/lib/llm.ts` (`generateStructuredJson`, `llmFlashModel`). Do not introduce Vercel AI SDK (`ai`, `@ai-sdk/*`) unless the AI SDK review doc is updated with an approved migration slice.
5. **Daily:** Transcription is Deepgram-backed via Daily (`startTranscription`, WebVTT storage). Translation is AstroLink-owned — Daily does not translate.
6. **Audit:** Log translation jobs to `audit_log` with `agent_id: APX-06`, `segment_id`, `source_locale`, `target_locale`, and `token_estimate`.
7. **UI:** Live captions must work at 320px width; follow `skills/mobile-first-design-practices/SKILL.md`.
8. **Scope guard:** D3 v1 is in-session captions + post-session recap translation — not full-app i18n (that is a separate initiative).

## Phase gates

| Phase | Ship criteria |
|-------|---------------|
| 1 Capture | WebVTT stored; APX-03 receives real transcript window |
| 2 Recap i18n | `preferred_locale` recap renders for ≥2 locales |
| 3 Live captions | Sub-2s caption latency in demo; glossary spot-check pass |

## Aerospace glossary

Technical terms in `src/lib/transcript-translation/glossary.ts` must pass through translation unchanged. Update glossary when onboarding experts in new domains (launch, propulsion, policy).
